SUMMARY:Panigiri of Ai-Giannis Nistevtis\, Faros
LOCATION:Faros\, Sifnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:For the Beheading of St John (29 August) Sifnos has five Ai-Giannis feasts on the evening of the 28th — Choni\, Mavro Chorio\, Siderou\, Mangana — but the easiest for visitors is Ai-Giannis 'the Faster' at Faros\, a chapel above the beach\, which does its panigiri on the morning of the 29th after liturgy. Being a fast day\, the panigyras serves the Lenten menu: cod with cabbage salad instead of lamb\, alongside the revithada.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/sifnos/#faros-panigiri-of-ai-giannis-nistevtis-faros
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/sifnos/#faros-panigiri-of-ai-giannis-nistevtis-faros
